conductor-provisioner for Fedora and Basalt OS
=============================================

Installing the package creates the "conductor-provisioner" system user,
/etc/conductor-provisioner (root:conductor-provisioner 0750) with
credentials/ (root 0700), the configuration file
/etc/conductor-provisioner/provisioner.toml (0640) and
/var/lib/conductor-provisioner. It does not enable or start anything.
Where the targeted SELinux policy is installed,
conductor-provisioner-selinux comes with it and the service runs in
conductor_provisioner_t.

  1. Install conductor first: the API socket's group is "conductor".
  2. Create the delegated account and delegate the managed OUs
     ("conductor-provisioner delegation preview --ou DN" prints the
     commands). Its password goes in credentials/account-password and a
     state key in credentials/state-key (both root, 0600):
       sudo sh -c 'umask 077; openssl rand -hex 32 > /etc/conductor-provisioner/credentials/state-key'
     Keep a copy of the state key with your backups.
  3. The domain CA in /etc/conductor-provisioner/domain-ca.pem; edit
     provisioner.toml (realm, account, scope OUs, conductor's role group
     SIDs).
  4. Start it:
       sudo systemctl enable --now conductor-provisioner-api.socket conductor-provisioner.service
  5. Enable the provisioner section in conductor's configuration.

Upgrades restart the service when it is running. "dnf remove
conductor-provisioner" stops and disables the units and removes the
packaged files; it keeps the credentials (account password, state key),
/var/lib/conductor-provisioner (tokens, audit log), the system user, and
the delegation in AD and the account.

Full guide: https://github.com/openbasalt/samba-conductor-provisioner/blob/main/docs/install.md
